MAPPING_SEMANTICS §0 says quality can describe grounding establishment or stored-label fit, then distinguishes primary-label, unique-synonym and unique-CAS resolution. The same baseline's `sssom_grading.py` explicitly distinguishes string equality from judgment. A canonical label copied after substantive disambiguation cannot by itself erase the method that established the identity. Conversely, ordinary verification of an already lexically resolved entity does not automatically convert every mapping into manual curation.

The mapping-quality value MANUAL_CURATION is the existing method vocabulary, as explicitly used in #1258/#1263. It is separate from human-only `MappingEvidence.evidence_type=MANUAL_CURATION` under #1226. Preserve historical evidence types and append truthful LLM_SUGGESTION/agent-assisted history where appropriate. Do not claim a human supplied or verified new evidence.

## Evidence and distinctions

**Borax.** The exact final source decision and history explicitly replace the contradictory CHEBI:131366 representation only after primary formula accounting. Captured [IUCr study](https://journals.iucr.org/e/issues/2008/05/00/wm2174/wm2174.pdf) (`e23bf55e…`, original web extraction including its source URL and page/line provenance) identifies conventional borax decahydrate with the hydroxylated tetraborate structural formula and eight molecular waters. The official CHEBI:38888 capture `6933410e…` supplies matching formula/mass; Sigma S9640 `da1665a2…` corroborates conventional formula/CAS. This is not a license to treat arbitrary octahydrate and decahydrate formulas as equivalent. The source-shared MediaDive ID and DSMZ770 stock remain limited. The exact chemistry was already recorded in [#318's source decision](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/318#issuecomment-6717638910); its three UW reference corrections remain under #1168. Neither is a new method approval.

**Sulfur.** The verified baseline `d3c21491…` already has CURATOR_JUDGMENT, CHEBI:33403 and history[16] for [#368](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/368). The new union does not alter that method. Official ChEBI capture `807c96cb…` names elemental sulfur; the sole captured synonym is elemental sulphur. DSMZ1092/854/897 captures `8b4c6b81…`, `a295f871…`, `68264077…` show weighed powder and separate handling. This supports material scope, not a new allotrope/structure/lot assertion. A correct retained explanatory comment would not repair the method field by itself. C authored later compatible-delta Sulfur composition, so this triage does not constitute distinct full-payload approval of those authored bytes; W09's independent method assessment remains separately bound.

**Diarsenic.** The original author-draft-v1 decision had no proposal while the empirical/molecular representation concern remained. The final decision and owner then explicitly resolve that concern through the ChEBI 2:3 definition (`7c89e661…`) and PubChem empirical formula (`2000d6d0…`). Primary [CCAP UCM](https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_UCM.pdf) (`29ffa570…`) distinguishes the oxide reagent from its alkaline preparation. Exact identity CHEBI:30621 remains supported at this declared scope; neither a stock nor arsenite is substituted.

W09's assertion that no unique-synonym lookup was recorded needs qualification. Actual capture `5f9314de…` is an executed OLS query `q=As2O3&exact=true&rows=30` with seven results, one defining ChEBI result, CHEBI:30621. Other entries include imported copies and other ontologies. As2O3 is a related synonym, which is not automatically a false identity synonym: [#317's clarification](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317#issuecomment-5383754233) explicitly notes that scope distinction. This real search can support resolution, but the final decisive representation adjudication is affirmative evidence for the manual-method recommendation. SYNONYM_MATCH is an alternative only after an accountable reassessment of the actual sufficient resolution, preserving both traces; it is not mandated merely by finding the string. No extra primary research is needed to acknowledge the existing search.

**Benzene-triol.** Official primary capture `03c17e8a…` names benzene-1,2,4-triol and includes the source spelling 1,2,4-trihydroxybenzene. Archived DSMZ799 `55deda68…` prints that source name. The retained decision states matching substitution pattern, but unlike Borax/Diarsenic/Sulfur records no affirmative conflicting CAS or representation choice. EXACT_MATCH may reflect actual primary-label resolution/fit; the precise lookup route is not explicit. Keep a qualified method assessment rather than assert a false identity, fabricate a lookup, or force a manual grade solely from LLM authorship.

## Routing and correction bounds

Recommended existing tracker: [#1201](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201), whose [TAPS comment](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201#issuecomment-6719419310) already covers source-proposal method provenance. Link #318/#368 for retained identity decisions and #317/#519 for grade/producer context. #1226 is the separate human-evidence issue; #1258 and #1263 are analogous ancillary cases, not these three owners. Live bounded all-state searches and the specified bodies/comments were captured; this is not an exhaustive comment crawl. Root decides filing.

After filing, any authorized correction should preserve original complete payloads/history, change only justified method/evidence/history fields, and receive distinct exact-byte and full-row review. The native builder maps MANUAL_CURATION to ManualMappingCuration and method-grade 0.9 while its final own-identifier override retains skos:exactMatch. Do not hand-edit SSSOM, weaken predicates, or interpret 0.9 as a measured probability. Source/date/comment and old validation stamps require full-row review after an actual new generation. No native projection, prepare, source edit, restart, process signal, Git mutation, paid provider or GitHub write occurred here.

This is a concise issue-triage packet, not a new native saved review pair or final application/export approval. The original W09 finding IDs and provisional status are preserved. Root owns the held transaction and any guarded successor route.
